>>> PROVEN: the ledger retains milestone 1's full artifacts (including the diff that names the exact symbol 'SETTINGS'), but pack_prompt() -- the ONLY code path that turns frozen_context() into what a delegated executor actually reads -- renders JUST the planner-authored description for every completed milestone, never its artifacts/diff/output. Milestone 3's executor is asked to 'import the settings dict created in milestone create-settings-module' with NO WAY to know the dict is named SETTINGS (vs CONFIG, APP_SETTINGS, or anything else) short of independently re-reading the repo itself. Any multi-milestone plan where a later milestone depends on a concrete, execution-time-decided fact from an earlier one has NO guaranteed prompt-level path for that fact to survive -- the executor either has to rediscover it (only possible if it has filesystem tool access, e.g. tier-0 ReAct's read_file, and only if it thinks to look; CodexAdapter with cwd=None can't even do that reliably, see the separate cwd-wiring finding) or it silently guesses wrong.
